{"equiv": "N","explanation": "Q1 and Q2 are not semantically equivalent because Q1 explicitly joins the PERSON and ADDRESS tables on the PERSONID column, while Q2 uses a NATURAL LEFT JOIN, which automatically joins tables on all columns with the same names, potentially leading to unintended results if there are columns with the same name in different tables.","counterexample_dsp": "The difference will be triggered if there are columns with the same name in both PERSON and ADDRESS tables, and the data in these columns is different.","counterexample": "INSERT INTO PERSON (PERSONID, FIRSTNAME, LASTNAME) VALUES (1, 'John', 'Doe');
